  "body": "From https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=953169#c9\r\n\r\n> I see, thanks. It's not clear to me it's necessarily a bug - the focus doesn't cause the scroll, the IME does, though I can see how one might expect it not to. I think not scrolling in this case could have some UX issues on mobile devices that we'd need to think through. Unless there's demand and reasonable use cases, I'm inclined to WontFix for now\r\n\r\nChrome ignores `preventscroll` option of `focus()` when android device has on screen keyboard (OSK).  If this option of `focus()` is ignored when OSK is used, we should add an exception on spec.  But I don't agree that this options is ignored even if device has OSK.\r\n\r\nCC: @mbrodesser",
